# Ingestion configuration — template.
#
# Copy to `ingestion_config.yaml`, which is gitignored because an exclusion list
# names client repositories. Without the copy there are no exclusions at all, and
# nothing says so: `load_exclusions` treats a missing file as an empty set and
# logs at DEBUG. A fresh clone therefore ingests everything.
#
# Read by `RepoLifecycle.load_exclusions`. Only `exclude` is consumed.

# Repositories the daily incremental run skips entirely, by `owner/name`.
#
# Exclusion FREEZES a repo; it does not remove it. `process_repo` returns
# `excluded` before it fetches, so documents the repo already has stay in the
# corpus at whatever commit they were last ingested at and drift from then on.
# They are not orphan-deleted either: that path compares the corpus against the
# canonical repo list, and excluding a repo does not take it off that list.
#
# Two different intentions, and this file only expresses one:
#   - "stop spending ingestion time on this"  -> add it here
#   - "get this out of search"                -> delete its documents as well
exclude: []
  # - owner/repo-name
